<section class="section" id="about">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div>
        <p class="folio">01</p>
        <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      </div>
      <h2 class="section-title reveal">
        Equal parts engineer and designer, with a curator’s habit of collecting
        things worth keeping.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="about-body">
      <p class="reveal">
        I design and build complete products — the SwiftUI screen you tap, the
        TypeScript service behind it, and the seams where the two meet. Most of
        what’s below I took from idea to shipped, usually on my own.
      </p>
      <p class="reveal">
        I care about the parts people feel but rarely name: the timing of a
        transition, the wording of an empty state, the weight of a headline. The
        collecting instinct spills past software, too — records, recipes, parts,
        ideas — and I have an enthusiast’s habit of going a little too deep on
        all of them.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .about-body {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin-left: auto;
  }
  @media (min-width: 48rem) {
    .about-body {
      margin-right: 0;
      /* align under the content column, past the index gutter */
      margin-left: calc(14rem + 2rem);
    }
  }
  .about-body p {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  .about-body p + p {
    margin-top: 1.4rem;
  }
</style>
